   "widgets_values": [
    "## Verboa still to MiniMax H3 clip\nThe whole pipeline in one graph: **Verboa Image 1.0** draws the first frame (8 steps, CFG 2, shift 4, empty negative), **MiniMax H3** animates it with **sound**, **Save clip** writes the mp4. The still is saved too (`output/Verboa/`).\n\n1. Write the picture in **First-frame prompt** (Verboa's short, direct caption style).\n2. Describe the same picture and what happens next in **H3 prompt** (format below).\n3. Press Run. A new still: change the Verboa seed. A new take of the same still: change the H3 seed (the still is cached).\n\nThe still is drawn at 768x1344 (9:16, the same shape as the clip) and scaled to the clip size; keep both shapes the same. Leave the negative prompt empty: Verboa was trained with the empty caption as its negative.\n\n**Defaults:** 512x896 (9:16), 6 s at 24 fps, 4 steps with the 4-step turbo LoRA (res_multistep, simple, Basic Guider). 768x1344 is H3's native 768p size: sharper, but more than twice the render time (2.25x the pixels). Width and height must be multiples of 32. The duration is rounded up to H3's frame grid (17k+5 frames at 24 fps): 6 s gives 158 frames.\n**Speed:** a laptop RTX 5090 (24 GB) with 64 GB of RAM renders an 8 s clip at 512x896 in about 110 s once the models are loaded (ComfyUI 0.37.4).\n\n### The H3 prompt format\nH3 reads labelled sections. Keep the labels and the blank lines between them:\n- **Header:** `For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.` `<Picture 1>` is your first frame.\n- **integrated_multimodal_description:** start with `[Shot 1]` and the look of the footage (camera, light), then `At 00:00.000 a medium shot holds the exact starting frame from <Picture 1>: ...` describing the picture as it is. Then one time-coded beat per action (`From 00:02.000 she ...`), and end with `The shot ends at 00:06.000.` Keep every time code inside the duration. A cut: `[Shot 2] At 00:04.000 hard cut to ...`. A spoken line: `The woman with a soft voice (S1) says: <d>[English] Hi.</d>`\n- **overall_soundscape:** everything you hear (room tone, steps, voices). H3 generates the sound in the same pass as the picture.\n- **non_diegetic_music:** music that is not part of the scene, or `N/A`.\n\nTips: a first frame with the subject facing the camera and fully in view animates best; plain sentences with time codes work better than tag lists; handheld phone footage reads as real.\n\n### More LoRAs\nChain extra H3 LoRAs (motion, style or NSFW LoRAs made for H3 FL2V) after **Turbo LoRA**: add a *LoraLoaderModelOnly* node per LoRA and connect the last one's MODEL to **Basic Guider** and **Scheduler**. Keep the turbo LoRA at 1.0 with 4 steps unless a LoRA's author says otherwise, and put trigger words at the very start of the prompt."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  },
